### ClearWood Furnitures — Prompt 8: cart, wishlist, addresses and recently-viewed
### VS Code REST Client. Runs top to bottom; @variables carry state forward.
###
### The story: a guest configures two sofas, applies a coupon, checks delivery, saves one for
### later, then logs in — and their guest cart merges into the account cart with a clear report
### while the totals still match /pricing/quote to the paise.

@host = http://localhost:7180
@api = {{host}}/api/v1
@email = aarav.mehta@example.com
@password = CustomerDemo@2026

### ------------------------------------------------------- as a guest

### 1. An empty cart. Note: this sets NO cookie — a read must never mint a guest identity.
# @name emptyCart
GET {{api}}/cart

### 2. Find the sofa we are going to configure, and its variants.
# @name sofa
GET {{api}}/catalog/products/kabir-3-seater-fabric-sofa

@productId = {{sofa.response.body.data.id}}
@beigeCotton = {{sofa.response.body.data.variants.0.id}}
@beigeVelvet = {{sofa.response.body.data.variants.1.id}}

### 3. Add the Beige / Cotton sofa. THIS is the request that mints the httpOnly `cw_cart` cookie.
# @name firstAdd
POST {{api}}/cart/items
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "variantId": "{{beigeCotton}}", "qty": 1 }

@lineId = {{firstAdd.response.body.data.lines.0.id}}

### 4. Add the Beige / Velvet sofa — a DIFFERENT lineKey, so a second line.
POST {{api}}/cart/items
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "variantId": "{{beigeVelvet}}", "qty": 1 }

### 5. Add Beige / Cotton again — the SAME lineKey, so qty becomes 2 rather than a third line.
POST {{api}}/cart/items
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "variantId": "{{beigeCotton}}", "qty": 1 }

### 6. Read it back: two lines, a full PriceBreakdown, issues and priceChanges.
# @name guestCart
GET {{api}}/cart

### 7. Delivery promise for Mumbai. City, zone and ETA all come from the Prompt 6 shipping tables.
PUT {{api}}/cart/pincode
Content-Type: application/json

{ "pincode": "400001" }

### 8. Apply the seeded welcome coupon.
POST {{api}}/cart/coupon
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "WELCOME10" }

### 9. PROOF OF PRICING AUTHORITY — this quote must match the cart's breakdown component by
### component: subtotal, discount, shipping, tax, rounding and grand total.
POST {{api}}/pricing/quote
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    { "productId": "{{productId}}", "variantId": "{{beigeCotton}}", "qty": 2 },
    { "productId": "{{productId}}", "variantId": "{{beigeVelvet}}", "qty": 1 }
  ],
  "couponCode": "WELCOME10",
  "pincode": "400001",
  "channel": "WEB"
}

### 10. Save a line for later — it leaves the total immediately.
POST {{api}}/cart/items/{{lineId}}/save-for-later

### 11. And bring it back.
POST {{api}}/cart/items/{{lineId}}/move-to-cart

### 12. Move it to the wishlist instead.
POST {{api}}/cart/items/{{lineId}}/move-to-wishlist
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 13. A tiny payload for the header badge.
GET {{api}}/cart/summary

### --------------------------------------------------- validation

### 14. Validate the deliberately broken seeded cart's shape of problems: OUT_OF_STOCK and
### MAX_QTY_EXCEEDED arrive as coded, human-readable issues.
POST {{api}}/cart/validate

### 15. Same call with autoFix — quantities are clamped and the fixes are reported, never silent.
POST {{api}}/cart/validate?autoFix=true

### ------------------------------------------------------ logging in

### 16. Log in. The guest cart merges into the account cart INSIDE this request — there is no
### second auth path and no separate merge call in the happy path.
# @name login
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "identifier": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 17. The merged cart. The guest lines are now on the customer cart; quantities were summed.
GET {{api}}/cart

### 18. The explicit merge endpoint, for clients that need the report itself. Idempotent: run it
### twice and the second call answers `merged: false` without touching a thing.
POST {{api}}/cart/merge
Content-Type: application/json

{ "strategy": "SUM_QUANTITIES" }

### ------------------------------------------------------- addresses

### 19. Pincode autofill + serviceability in one call — the form and the cart cannot disagree.
GET {{api}}/addresses/pincode/400001

### 20. A pincode no seeded zone covers.
GET {{api}}/addresses/pincode/682555

### 21. The seeded address book.
GET {{api}}/me/addresses

### 22. Add an address, letting the pincode fill in the city and state.
# @name newAddress
POST {{api}}/me/addresses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "Weekend house",
  "type": "OTHER",
  "usage": "SHIPPING",
  "fullName": "Aarav Mehta",
  "phone": "919810000001",
  "line1": "7 Hill Road, Lonavala",
  "city": "Pune",
  "state": "Maharashtra",
  "stateCode": "MH",
  "pincode": "411001"
}

@addressId = {{newAddress.response.body.data.id}}

### 23. Make it the default. Exactly one default per usage survives.
POST {{api}}/me/addresses/{{addressId}}/default?usage=SHIPPING

### 24. Soft delete — the row survives so Prompt 9's orders can still point at it.
DELETE {{api}}/me/addresses/{{addressId}}

### -------------------------------------------------------- wishlists

### 25. Lists, with live prices and price-drop flags.
# @name lists
GET {{api}}/wishlists

@listId = {{lists.response.body.data.0.id}}

### 26. Share it.
# @name shared
POST {{api}}/wishlists/{{listId}}/share

### 27. Open the share link as a stranger — no session, and no customer identity in the payload.
GET {{api}}/wishlists/shared/{{shared.response.body.data.shareToken}}

### 28. Stop sharing. The token 404s immediately afterwards.
DELETE {{api}}/wishlists/{{listId}}/share

### -------------------------------------------------- recently viewed

### 29. What this shopper has been looking at.
GET {{api}}/me/recently-viewed?limit=12

### 30. Clear it.
DELETE {{api}}/me/recently-viewed

### ------------------------------------------------------------ admin

### 31. Admin login (ORDER_MANAGER or above; `order.customer.read` is the gate).
# @name adminLogin
POST {{api}}/admin/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@clearwood.local", "password": "ChangeMe@2026" }

### 32. Live and abandoned carts.
GET {{api}}/admin/carts?limit=20

### 33. Abandoned only — the recovery list.
GET {{api}}/admin/carts?status=ABANDONED

### 34. Lifecycle totals, abandonment rate and the most-abandoned products.
GET {{api}}/admin/carts/stats

### 35. Most-wishlisted products and the price-drop watch list.
GET {{api}}/admin/wishlists/stats

### 36. The cleanup sweep: ACTIVE -> ABANDONED -> EXPIRED. It never deletes a shopper's lines.
POST {{api}}/admin/carts/cleanup
Content-Type: application/json

{}
